  "id": "COMPOUND:30640 - PROTEIN:5805",
  "verbalization": "Alpneumine H appears to have a shared target of Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, which is subsequently targeted by multiple compounds, including Yuanhunine, Flavipin, and Pseudopterosin Q. All these compounds ultimately target SCCH-26, suggesting a potential pathway where Alpneumine H may exert its effects through a common mechanism involving Thioredoxin, mitochondrial. The evidence indicates that Alpneumine H may act by modulating Thioredoxin, mitochondrial activity, which in turn influences SCCH-26. The overlapping targets suggest a possible functional relationship, though the exact mechanism by which Alpneumine H interacts with Thioredoxin, mitochondrial, or SCCH-26 remains to be elucidated. The integration of these pathways highlights a potential role for Alpneumine H in modulating cellular processes that are relevant to SCCH-26, though further experimental validation is needed to confirm the precise nature of this interaction.",
